From bc6de13d10b9b29407b2fc86fd95d4fe5122b993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VortexStudio Contributor <contributor@example.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 19:38:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add startup dialog: New/Open/recent-projects, format picker

- StartupDialog shown before the main window with New Project, Open...,
  a recent-files list, and an Open-as format picker (Auto-detect /
  vBird Project / Vortex Studio Legacy) since project files from the
  original Vortex Studio may need to load here too eventually.
- RecentProjects reads/writes recent_projects.json under the standard
  Qt app-data location, deduping on reopen and capping at 10 entries.
- app.cpp shows the dialog first and sets the window title from the
  selection; actual project parsing is left as a TODO for whoever
  builds the loader.

Kept deliberately minimal per request: no icons, no format
auto-detection, no project parsing yet.

Built and tested locally against Qt 6.4/CMake/Ninja: clean build with
no warnings under -Wall -Wextra, RecentProjects covered by a standalone
unit test (add/dedupe/remove/JSON round-trip), StartupDialog rendered
headless to confirm layout/population.
